---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ContinueReading from "../components/ContinueReading.astro";
import { pageMeta } from "../data/pages";
import { LINKEDIN } from "../data/site";

const meta = pageMeta("work");
---
<BaseLayout {...meta} active="work" bodyClass={meta.bodyClass}>
  <section class="page-intro" aria-labelledby="work-page-title">
    <h1 id="work-page-title">Work, from prototypes to production.</h1>
    <p>I help robotics teams turn working systems into dependable production deployments.
      Explore ways to work together, the experience behind them, and what to expect.</p>
    <nav class="chapter-nav" aria-label="Work sections"><a href="#expertise">Ways to work together</a><a href="#exp">Experience</a><a href="#faq">Questions</a></nav>
  </section>

  <section class="section expertise-section" id="expertise" aria-labelledby="expertise-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <h2 id="expertise-title">How I can help your robotics team.</h2>
        <p>For robotics founders and CTOs in the EU and US building dependable
          production fleets. Work directly with me through a focused assessment,
          a delivery engagement, or ongoing technical leadership.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="engagement-options">
      <article class="engagement-option" aria-labelledby="assessment-title">
        <h3 id="assessment-title">Deployment Readiness Assessment</h3>
        <p>Before committing to the next rollout, get a clear view of
          deployment risk, engineering priorities, and the work required
          to scale.</p>
        <ul class="engagement-scope" aria-label="Assessment scope">
          <li>Release-to-robot workflow map</li>
          <li>Prioritized risks and operational gaps</li>
          <li>Sequenced implementation roadmap</li>
          <li>Findings reviewed with your engineers</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="button primary-button" href={LINKEDIN}
          aria-label="Discuss an assessment on LinkedIn">Discuss an assessment <span class="arrow diagonal" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="engagement-option" aria-labelledby="engineering-title">
        <h3 id="engineering-title">Production deployment engineering</h3>
        <p>For a defined delivery mandate. I work with your engineers to
          design and build the infrastructure behind repeatable,
          recoverable production deployments.</p>
        <ul class="engagement-scope" aria-label="Engineering scope">
          <li>Release automation and deployment pipelines</li>
          <li>Over-the-air updates, monitoring, and recovery</li>
          <li>Integration with your existing infrastructure</li>
          <li>Documentation and engineering handover</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="button primary-button" href={LINKEDIN}
          aria-label="Discuss implementation on LinkedIn">Discuss implementation <span class="arrow diagonal" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="engagement-option" aria-labelledby="leadership-title">
        <h3 id="leadership-title">Fractional Robotics DevOps leadership</h3>
        <p>For founders and CTOs who need ongoing senior technical direction.
          Align deployment strategy with customer commitments,
          infrastructure costs, and your team’s capacity to deliver.</p>
        <ul class="engagement-scope" aria-label="Leadership scope">
          <li>Technical roadmap and investment priorities</li>
          <li>Architecture and infrastructure-cost reviews</li>
          <li>Release and operational standards</li>
          <li>Agreed decision ownership and delivery milestones</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="button primary-button" href={LINKEDIN}
          aria-label="Discuss leadership on LinkedIn">Discuss leadership <span class="arrow diagonal" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="engagement-context">
      <p>Experience includes delivery infrastructure supporting <strong>more than 1,500 production robots</strong> at NODE Robotics. <a href="#earlier-work">Explore the experience behind the work</a>.</p>
      <p>Each engagement is scoped individually. We agree the mandate,
        deliverables, access, timing, and fees before starting.
        Assessment and implementation are separate engagements.</p>
    </div>
    <details class="technical-scope">
      <summary>
        <span class="scope-summary-copy">
          <span class="scope-summary-title">Technical capabilities</span> <span class="scope-summary-description">From code to fleet operations.</span>
        </span> <span class="scope-summary-action" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="scope-show">View details</span> <span class="scope-hide">Hide details</span> <span class="plus"></span>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <dl class="expertise-list">
      <div>
        <dt>Release engineering</dt>
        <dd>ROS / ROS 2 pipelines for building, testing, packaging, and releasing
          software, with reproducible environments and versioned artifacts.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Fleet deployment &amp; updates</dt>
        <dd>Staged over-the-air updates, compatibility checks, and recovery
          paths across on-premise, hybrid, and cloud-connected fleets.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Monitoring &amp; incident response</dt>
        <dd>Fleet logs, metrics, and dashboards that surface failures and
          rollout health, with clear workflows for diagnosis and recovery.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Infrastructure &amp; architecture</dt>
        <dd>Robot-to-cloud architecture shaped around reliability,
          infrastructure cost, and the people who operate and maintain
          your fleet.</dd>
      </div>
      </dl>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section class="section experience-section" id="exp" aria-labelledby="experience-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <h2 id="experience-title">Experience behind the work.</h2>
        <p>Robotics software, deployment infrastructure, and production operations.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <article class="experience-entry" id="current-work" aria-labelledby="current-experience-title">
      <header>
        <h3 id="current-experience-title">Stealth defense robotics startup</h3>
        <p class="experience-role">Current work · Software factory infrastructure</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/about.html#today">The story behind this work <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
      </header>
      <div class="experience-content">
        <p>I build the infrastructure connecting development, testing, release,
          and deployment—so the team can deliver and maintain robot software
          consistently.</p>
        <dl class="experience-detail">
          <div><dt>Release engineering</dt>
            <dd>CI/CD, release automation, and verification gates connecting
              code changes to controlled releases.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>In-house fleet updates</dt>
            <dd>Built the OTA system and led the engineering work behind
              its CE conformity.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Quality processes</dt>
            <dd>Led ISO 9001 and CE certification processes, aligning engineering
              workflows with quality requirements and supporting evidence.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Engineering visibility</dt>
            <dd>Release notes, delivery metrics, and coordination that make
              progress and changes visible across the team.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="experience-entry" id="earlier-work" aria-labelledby="node-experience-title">
      <header>
        <h3 id="node-experience-title">NODE Robotics</h3>
        <p class="experience-role">Robotics DevOps &amp; infrastructure leadership</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://node-robotics.com/">About NODE Robotics <span class="arrow diagonal" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
      </header>
      <div class="experience-content">
        <p>I led delivery infrastructure for production robot fleets across
          customer environments, connecting software changes to reliable deployments.</p>
        <ul class="experience-results">
          <li>Infrastructure supporting <strong>more than 1,500 production robots</strong>.</li>
          <li>Provisioning and deployment workflows supporting <strong>three software releases a month</strong>.</li>
          <li>A hybrid on-premises/VPC architecture that <strong>reduced infrastructure costs by 50%</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
        <figure class="experience-recommendation">
          <blockquote>“He is an expert with Ansible and other deployment tooling.”</blockquote>
          <figcaption><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/philipp-schnattinger-5341b8110/">Philipp Schnattinger</a> · CRO, NODE Robotics <span><a href={LINKEDIN}>Read the recommendation on LinkedIn</a></span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="experience-entry" aria-labelledby="robotair-experience-title">
      <header>
        <h3 id="robotair-experience-title">Robotair</h3>
        <p class="experience-role">Founder · Robotics DevOps infrastructure</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://robotair.io/">Explore Robotair <span class="arrow diagonal" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
      </header>
      <div class="experience-content">
        <p>I founded Robotair to connect robot application packaging,
          over-the-air updates, and fleet monitoring. A 12-month beta reached <strong>15 paying customers</strong> across Europe and India.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="experience-entry" aria-labelledby="fraunhofer-experience-title">
      <header>
        <h3 id="fraunhofer-experience-title">Fraunhofer IPA / ROS-Industrial</h3>
        <p class="experience-role">Robotics research &amp; system integration</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://www.ipa.fraunhofer.de/en.html">About Fraunhofer IPA <span class="arrow diagonal" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
      </header>
      <div class="experience-content">
        <p>I developed and deployed ROS 2 systems with industrial partners,
          built CI/CD workflows, and delivered ROS-Industrial training to
          help teams operate the systems themselves.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section story-bridge" id="projects" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
    <h2 id="projects-title">Where my engineering approach began.</h2>
    <p>Follow the journey from university rovers to industrial deployments and
      production fleets, with the projects that shaped how I work.</p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/about.html#origins">Read my story <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
  </section>

  <section class="section faq-section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <div class="section-heading" id="process">
      <div>
        <h2 id="faq-title">Questions about working together.</h2>
        <p>Clarity on fit, scope, and ownership before an engagement begins.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <article class="faq-item" aria-labelledby="faq-fit">
      <h3 id="faq-fit">When is your involvement most valuable?</h3>
      <p>When deployment is becoming a constraint on the business: pilots are
        moving into customer environments, fleets are expanding, or release
        and recovery work depends on a few people. I focus on the infrastructure
        and engineering practices needed to make that next stage repeatable.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="faq-item" aria-labelledby="faq-engagement">
      <h3 id="faq-engagement">Which engagement should we start with?</h3>
      <p>Start with an <strong>assessment</strong> to clarify risks and priorities, <strong>production engineering</strong> to deliver an agreed system, or <strong>fractional leadership</strong> for ongoing technical direction.
        We choose the engagement around the outcome you need.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="faq-item" aria-labelledby="faq-collaboration">
      <h3 id="faq-collaboration">How will you work with our engineering team?</h3>
      <p>I work with your engineers on the agreed scope, using your robot platform,
        deployment environment, and existing workflows as the starting point.
        We define access, decision-making responsibilities, and review milestones
        upfront, so ownership is clear throughout the engagement.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="faq-item" aria-labelledby="faq-commercials">
      <h3 id="faq-commercials">How are timing and fees determined?</h3>
      <p>Each engagement is scoped individually. The work required, system
        complexity, access, and level of involvement shape the proposal.
        We agree deliverables, milestones, responsibilities, and fees before
        starting; implementation and ongoing leadership are scoped separately
        from an assessment.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="faq-item" aria-labelledby="faq-handover">
      <h3 id="faq-handover">What happens at handover?</h3>
      <p>Implementation includes documentation and an engineering handover,
        covering the key decisions and workflows your team needs to operate
        and maintain the system. We agree handover expectations and any
        ongoing support as part of the scope.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="faq-item" aria-labelledby="faq-robotair">
      <h3 id="faq-robotair">How does this relate to Robotair?</h3>
      <p>I founded Robotair. This page describes working directly with me on
        deployment engineering and technical leadership. For a Robotair-specific
        inquiry, mention the product in your message so we can clarify the scope.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <ContinueReading
    heading="Let’s talk about what you’re building."
    description="Tell me about your robot platform, the deployment challenge you’re facing, and your next milestone. We can start by discussing fit and the right scope."
    href="/writing.html"
    label="Explore my engineering notes"
  />
</BaseLayout>
